+ "$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
+ "$id":"https://goldkelch.github.io/qik-vrt/schemas/temdd-ir-v0.1.schema.json",
+ "title":"TEMDD canonical IR v0.1","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,
+ "required":["schema","version","authority","subject","request","handlers","dod"],
+ "properties":{
+  "schema":{"const":"temdd_ir_v0_1"},"version":{"const":"0.1"},"authority":{"type":"string","minLength":1},
+  "subject":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["name","repository","binding"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"repository":{"type":"string"},"binding":{"const":"exact"}}},
+  "request":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["name","target"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"target":{"type":"string"}}},
+  "handlers":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["event","statements"],"properties":{"event":{"enum":["event","blocker"]},"statements":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}},
+  "dod":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string"}}
+ }
+}
diff --git a/spec/temdd/README.md b/spec/temdd/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..dfaee7bdb1ab1531db01f839dab8a8618c3469c1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/spec/temdd/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# TEMDD
+
+Tested Event Model Driven Development is specified here as an executable QIK-VRT metaprogramming language.
+
+Entry points:
+- `TEMDD_LANGUAGE_SPEC_V0_1.md` — normative bootstrap semantics.
+- `TEMDD_Syntax_V0_1.ebnf` — grammar.
+- `../../schemas/temdd-ir-v0.1.schema.json` — canonical IR contract.
+- `../../tools/qikvrt_temdd.py` — deterministic reference parser/elaborator.
+- `../../tools/qikvrt_temdd_conformance.py` — executable T01-T12 semantic checks.
+- `../../tests/temdd/` — positive and fail-closed negative corpus.
+- `../../runtime/temdd/TEMDDRuntime.st` — Smalltalk live-object backend bootstrap.
+- `../../src/temdd_core.c` — C90 deterministic backend.
+- `../../runtime/m68000/temdd_transition.s` — fixed-relation M68000 backend bootstrap.
+- `../../formalization/TEMDDCore.lean` — formal semantic obligations.
+- `../../examples/temdd/qikvrt_convergence_v0_1.temdd` — first dogfood production program.
+
+Language evolution is itself TEMDD: mutation creates a new exact subject; predecessor validation does not transfer; the successor must pass fresh conformance and deployment readback.
diff --git a/spec/temdd/TEMDD_ARCHITECTURE_V0_1.md b/spec/temdd/TEMDD_ARCHITECTURE_V0_1.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..31c772a76c1e904e9211b7036570df953698156b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/spec/temdd/TEMDD_ARCHITECTURE_V0_1.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# TEMDD architecture v0.1
+
+TEMDD is the single normative semantic core. Python, Smalltalk, C90, M68000, Lean, GitHub Actions and deployment systems are projections or adapters, not independent control-plane semantics.
+
+The architecture is layered: language source; deterministic frontend; canonical typed IR; semantic conformance; backend projections; transport adapters; effect executors; readback observers. Only the semantic core decides status. Transport layers may deliver events but may not synthesize authority, evidence, DONE or EFFECT_ACK.
+
+This separation permits gradual replacement of duplicated Python/YAML control logic while preserving observable behavior through shared vectors and exact-subject evidence.
